scapes  and then it's time for the sarlacc pit  now i couldn't help during this scene  but think  sand worm sand worm sand or and it's  kind of like a sand worm  but it's not really a sand worm it's  just kind of like this  pit thing with tentacles so jabba the  hut is gonna it's gonna throw  luke into into the pit and it's really  really tense  but then luke pulls a fast one and he's  actually hitting his lightsaber  inside of r2d2 so luke frees himself and  starts fighting with  boba fett now i know a lot of people  always talk about boba fett and how cool  he is  but i really don't get it boba fett is  not that cool  from what i've seen i don't know if he  shows up in other stuff but so far like  i don't really get the obsession with  boba fett  i asked on twitter like what's the deal  with boba fett and no one i don't i  don't know  what the deal is i don't know but anyway  while luke is battling this guy  something way more interesting happens  with leia leia  grabs her chains and strangles [ __ ]  jabba the hutt to death  leia strangles jabba the hutt i was not  expecting her to strangle him to death  that is some brutal [ __ ] holy [ __ ] lair  i love leia leia is like my favorite  like i said in my other review for  empire strikes back she's such a badass  she's a boss she's like yeah you got me  in chains right now but i'm gonna  strangle you to death with these chains  when i get a chance and she does  freaking awesome so the whole sequence  of jabba the hut in the beginning was  super exciting it was fun it's a little  bit on the silly side but a lot of the  star wars stuff is on the silly side so  i can't really knock it for that  it was a lot of fun i enjoyed watching  it so after all that goes down luke goes  back to dagobah  and we have this really sad sequence  where  yoda dies and i kind of didn't want yoda  to die  i really thought he would be around for  a little bit longer i felt like i didn't  get enough of  master yoda and he was in empire strikes  back and then he's gone in this one but  then i guess what did i really expect it  was the completion of a trilogy  a curious thing that i've noticed that  star wars has done  is they do the death of the mentor twice  if you count a new hope  obi-wan's death and yoda's death in this  movie  and then curiously enough obi-wan shows  up in this scene as well so they're  definitely  calling back echoing what they did in  the first movie intentionally i think  but anyway yoda dies but not before  telling luke that he already  has everything he needs to succeed and  then obi-wan kenobi's ghost  offers the information that leia  is luke's sister and that he has to go  and find darth vader and defeat him and  resist the emperor in order to complete  his training and become a jedi  so wow a while ago i did a comparison on  star wars  to dune which i researched without  actually watching the movies  and i kind of forgot a lot of the  information the time since doing  that video so having this revelation  come into play was kind of like an oh  yeah moment they're basically latoya  ganima  all right moving on so the alliance  learns that the empire is constructing a  new death star  but they have to take down the shield  before they can attack it and the shield  generator is on the forest moon  of indoor and on the forest moon of  indore we encounter the  ewoks who are like these crazy hairy  little  alien guys they're super goofy and super  weird and funny  uh i really thought the scene was really  funny when they think that c3po is like  some kind of god  that's such a funny thing that happens  in sci-fi  one of my favorite star trek episodes  who watches the watchers  is kind of like a more serious take on  that and you know even like the dune  thing with the freeman is like a way  more serious take on that but you know  that idea  that when technology becomes advanced  enough it seems  god-like or magical to you know  primitive people that haven't seen that  before  so anyway first the ewoks are going to  kill the group and then they start  thinking that c-3po is god so they  decide not to  so the movie takes a very interesting  turn  after luke reveals to leia that  they are brother and sister and  luke goes off and  surrenders to imperial troops and allows  himself to be taken into darth vader  and he tries to to to tempt darth vader  back to the good side  he thinks there is still good in darth  vader  and darth vader says it's too late for  me son and he takes him to the emperor  and we've been seeing the emperor bits  and pieces  throughout the movie but this  interaction with luke  darth vader and the emperor is where  this movie just  shines this is one of the best scenes  in any movie ever one of the best  sequences so as the alliance is on their  mission to  destroy the death star  luke is being tempted down the dark path  by the emperor who reveals that the  alliance is actually headed  into a trap and that this death star  isn't under construction this is a fully  functional  death star and it's capable of mass  destruction already  and all of your friends are gonna die  and he's like strike me down luke  strike me down in anger do it given to  your rage because he wants luke to give  in  he wants luke to lose control  obi-wan told him earlier to bury his  emotions down deep because they could be  used to tempt him  the jedi are all about mindfulness not  necessarily suppression  of emotions but mindfulness  of emotions controlling emotion the sith  are all about giving in to rage and  anger and even  fear it's consumption and chaos  versus balance and preservation so the  emperor is given the order to destroy  alliance ships  while luke witnesses it and it's too  much for him  he tries to swing on emperor  and then vader stops him and then  then we get an amazing lightsaber battle  now the one from the last movie darth  vader like  clearly was way better than luke luke  has learned  some things in the year or so since that  movie i see  in this movie the force is with luke and  he's  he's holding his own against darth vader  getting angry and anger kind of given  into his rage  he takes off darth vader's arm the  emperor comes up all like  yes give in to the dark side luke has  the chance to kill darth vader  then doesn't he say he can't do it  he says i will not puts down this  lightsaber  and the emperor is all like really  really mad and then the emperor is all  like now you will know the true power  off the dark side  freaking lightning comes out of his  hands  and he starts like zapping luke with  this messed up blue  lightning and he's all like it's like  where the frick did that come from  i like the idea of palpatine  having these powers that other people  don't have it's kind of like i know i  mentioned harry potter  in the last video but it's kind of like  how voldemort has like  tapped into all of these other magics  that other people don't know about  because he's  gone under the very very darkest corners  of magic that's what i  imagine that palpatine has done he's  like explore the dark corners of the  force  and he can do things that other people  can't do because he's palpatine  so anyways it looks like luke is done  like palpatine is like totally got him  with this lightning stuff  and then at the last minute darth vader  stops him he picks palpatine up and he  throws him off the thingamajig  saves his son darth vader could not  allow  his only son to be killed which is a  very very real thing  it's believable it's human because as  as as dark as darth vader was  as alien as he seems at time  as as evil as he seems at times as evil  as he certainly is he's killed  a lot of people he's still  ultimately a human and the human in him  could not bear to see his only son be  killed and that's just  strikes me as a very very true story so  luke goes up to his father he removes  his mask  for the first time we can we see darth  vader's face  he is dying and it's a very very  touching moment  and not at all what i really expected  from this movie i really thought that  this was going to end  with luke skywalker killing darth vader  it  subverted my expectations in the best  way sorry david and dan from game of  thrones  so after this the death star gets  destroyed again  and the heroes escape and luke  burns darth vader's body  on a pyre and says his final goodbyes to  his father  all right now to talk about something  that i know is  controversial amongst star wars fans  for some reason and it's kind of  surprising to me now before i watch this  movie  about a thousand people told me that i  was going to hate  the ewoks they said oh the ending with  the ewoks is so  stupid it makes no sense so at the end  of this movie we have  the ewoks helping our heroes overcome  the imperial like technology  walk things and you know helping them  defeat  the empire and their troops inside of  the forest  on the forest moon of endor apparently  a lot of people think this is really  silly surprisingly enough  i don't this totally would happen  you can look this up time and time again  throughout real world history this very  sort of thing  has happened you have technologically  superior invaders  coming into the land of a primitive  culture  and you know getting their asses kicked  this happens because  native societies tend to have  intimate connections with the land they  inhabit they know it  well they have the upper hand sometimes  superior technology just isn't enough  i remember in school we learned a story  of  british soldiers marching into the  territory  of native american tribes they were they  were marching to a battle and they had  these big drums and they were  marching out in the open the natives  ambushed them from the trees and  slaughtered them  you know the british soldiers certainly  had superior technology  but the natives knew their land so  actually i don't think the ewok thing is  stupid  little silly but no more silly than like  the jawas or the  sand people on tatooine i think it  actually fits  huh and you know another thing i like  this movie more than empire strikes back  this was my favorite of the three the  darth vader redemption arc was iconic  that was amazing that was such a great  scene  force lightning so good emperor  palpatine was so cool  when he said the death star is fully  functional i got chills  when he's all like now you will pay the  price for your lack of vision  i died that was so good i loved that  this movie  also had a lot of quiet moments between  characters  i loved the moments that luke and yoda  had in this movie even though it was  super sad  it was great the moment between luke and  leia was great the moments between  han and leia great a lot of people say  this movie's silly but i don't think  it's any more silly  than the rest of them i mean there was a  ridiculous  dance party that was like cgi and  clearly something that was like added  later i don't know what that was  supposed to be  but i'll kind of give them a break for  that i don't know how much of that was  in the original thing  i know these movies have been tampered  with the dance sequence was weird i will  give it that that was such a like  shift in tone i was like not ready i'm  like what is going on  but other than that like this movie was  fun i enjoyed it  if i had seen this when i was a kid i  would have loved it probably  i enjoyed it as an adult so here's the  thing i think this trilogy  for what it is is solid it's a good  trilogy  i think i think when taken as a whole  new hope  empire strikes back return of the jedi  it is a solid  movie trilogy new hope being the weak  link i think  empire strikes back and return of the  jedi clearly were two movies that were  thought about  together or at least i think they were  because they  they share themes and there's threads of  ideas that run through both of them  like when luke has his journey to the  innermost cave  which is actually a term used in joseph  campbell's book  about the hero's journey it's an  incident it's an actual step on the  hero's journey and luke  literally goes into a cave i thought  that scene was about  not striking down your enemy and anger  which was exactly what was going on in  this film return of the jedi it was  exactly that he was meant  not to strike down his enemy in anger  because that would have been giving in  to the dark side and that's not what the  jedi do and that's not who the jedi are  all right so a return of the jedi i  would say that between this one  and empire empire is great but i had  just a bit more fun watching this one so  i'll give this one  an 8.5 and i'll be moving on to watch  the star wars prequels which are very  controversial  um so these will be interesting to see  we'll see how it all started and the  beginnings of the empire and whatnot  and looks like yoda is doing some force  lightning on this so yoda can do the  forced lightning too  so that kind of like disproves my theory  about  palpatine doing dark things in the force  but maybe this movie sucks who knows  anyway thank you guys so much for  watching make sure you like and  subscribe for more of quinn's ideas

